From 17927586c13abc370477f6c00643959141319718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Li <lizhi.xmu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:12:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] deps: drop ngtcp2/nghttp3 (curl HTTP/3) from the build

They pull in curl's HTTP/3 stack, whose only Windows crypto backend here is openssl's QUIC.
openssl is pinned with GIT_RESET and patched through `git am --3way`; whenever that pin does
not land the freshly built openssl is a 4.x master without QUIC, and ngtcp2's configure then
aborts with 'Unable to build OpenSSL backend due to lack of QUIC support', failing the whole
build. Media playback needs HTTP/1.1 range requests only, so HTTP/3 is dead weight here:
curl keeps HTTP/1.1 + HTTP/2 (nghttp2) and the two packages are no longer built.
---
 packages/CMakeLists.txt | 2 --
 packages/curl.cmake     | 2 --
 2 files changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/CMakeLists.txt b/packages/CMakeLists.txt
index 1ada4b4..a0f6cad 100644
--- a/packages/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/packages/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -87,8 +87,6 @@ list(APPEND ep
     libaribcaption
     libsixel
     ffmpeg
-    ngtcp2
-    nghttp3
     nghttp2
     c-ares
     libpsl
diff --git a/packages/curl.cmake b/packages/curl.cmake
index 9e2130b..14c9b18 100644
--- a/packages/curl.cmake
+++ b/packages/curl.cmake
@@ -4,9 +4,7 @@ ExternalProject_Add(curl
         c-ares
         libpsl
         libssh
-        ngtcp2
         nghttp2
-        nghttp3
         openssl
         zlib
         zstd
-- 
2.45.1.windows.1

